# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# File policy: ignore an artifact ONLY when its regeneration is both offline AND
# cheap (seconds to ~a minute); anything needing the network, or costing
# GPU-hours, stays committed. Full rationale, the regeneration command and the
# MEASURED cost for every line below are in README.md ("File policy" + the
# decision log). Each "ignored" cost was measured by regenerating into a scratch
# path and comparing to the committed copy.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored (versioned): scenes/supermarket_base.blend and
# assets/textures/ (Poly Haven, network); report_assets/ (curated);
# scripts/planogram.json (small stage interface); renders/ and
# renders/walkthrough.mp4 (GPU-hours to render — the visible evidence);
# report.html (the human-facing deliverable that presents the renders).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Built scene — rebuilds in ~4 s, offline, from supermarket_base.blend + scripts:
#   blender -b scenes/supermarket_base.blend --python scripts/build_supermarket.py -- --all --save scenes/supermarket.blend
/scenes/supermarket.blend

# Generated labels, price tags and signs — ~6.7 s deterministic PIL output, offline:
#   python3 scripts/gen_labels.py
/assets/labels/
/assets/signs/

# USD export (usdc + its textures) — ~26 s, from the built scene:
#   blender -b scenes/supermarket.blend --python scripts/export_usd.py
/export/

# --- transient by nature ---------------------------------------------------

# Blender's rolling autosave backups: a byte-for-byte stale copy of the file
# next to it, regenerated on every save. 154 MB of pure duplication.
*.blend1

# Run logs. Useful while a build is in flight, meaningless once it has landed,
# and they grow without bound.
logs/

# Python bytecode from the generator scripts.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Throwaway CPU-only venv for the offline USD validator (scripts/validate_usd.py):
#   python3 -m venv .venv-usd && .venv-usd/bin/pip install usd-core   (offline, ~30 MB)
.venv-usd/
.venv/

# Reproducible CPU report embeds; source/evidence/generator remain versioned.
/data/mobile-restock-v2/report.html

# Throwaway venv for the offline scenario-generator tests + dataset validator:
#   uv venv --python 3.12 .venv-scenarios && uv pip install --python .venv-scenarios numpy pillow pytest
.venv-scenarios/

# Generated scenario datasets live OUTSIDE git (default ~/datasets/store-scenarios/);
# this guards against an in-repo --out by mistake. The committed smoke fixture under
# scripts/scenarios/tests/fixtures/ is deliberately NOT ignored.
/datasets/
/store-scenarios/
